'''arrow-grass''' (ar′ō-grȧs), ''n.'' A common name of plants of the genus ''Triglochin'', especially of the common ''T. palustre.'' {{smaller|It is also sometimes applied generally to the members of the tribe ''Juncagineæ'', to which ''Triglochin'' belongs, now usually included in the natural order ''Naiadaceæ.''}}

'''arrow-head''' (ar′ō-hed), ''n.'' and ''a.'' '''I.''' ''n.'' '''1.''' The head of an arrow.—'''2.''' An aquatic plant of the genus ''Sagittaria'': so called from the shape of the leaves. See ''Sagittaria.''—'''3.''' A belemnite.

'''II.''' ''a.'' Written with arrow-headed characters: as, an ''arrow-head'' inscription.

'''arrow-headed''' (ar′ō-hed″ed), ''a.'' Shaped like
